# Working documents — design specs, implementation plans, scratch notes.
#
# These are deliberately NOT tracked. Documentation that describes the system
# lives in the code as rustdoc (`//!` module docs and `///` item docs), so that
# it sits next to what it describes and goes stale loudly instead of quietly.
# See AGENTS.md. Anything in here that turns out to be worth keeping should be
# moved into module docs rather than committed as a separate file.
/docs/

# Local git worktrees for isolated feature work (superpowers:using-git-worktrees).
/.worktrees/
